    "answer": "Start with safe operator observations, keep a record of changes, and schedule qualified technician maintenance around the exact machine manual and duty cycle. New leaks, repeated faults, damaged safeguards, or unusual heat need prompt attention. Never bypass an interlock or perform hazardous work without training and energy isolation.",
